%description:

Tcp.delayedAckFrameCount:invalid -- a count below 1 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "at least 1". The code checks the value when a connection reads its
parameters (TcpConnection::initConnection()).

The classes: one (1), many (2 and more), invalid (0 and less).

Host under test: host2, whose listening connection reads the parameter. Observation: the
error at the open of the connection, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.delayedAckFrameCount
%# class: invalid
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host2.tcp.delayedAckFrameCount
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpDelayedAckFrameCountInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckFrameCount = 0    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
delayedAckFrameCount must be 1 or more, but it is 0
